# Weight profile nemotron-bolt-exl3-2.0-hq: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Bolt 74B-A9B in our EXL3 pack (ENG-337): routed experts
# at 2 bits, the Mamba2, attention, latent and shared-expert projections at 4, head 6 (exllamav3 1.6.2 with the
# Puzzle/Bolt patch, mul1 codebook; 23.41 GB, the RADIO tower kept in BF16 and not loaded), converted from
# nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-BF16 at revision bca0a8cb. The repository is private: the fetch uses the
# Hugging Face token. Measured 2026-10-15 against BF16 (8 wikitext rows x 1,024): KL 0.170, top-1 84.1 %
# (NVIDIA's IQ2 GGUF 0.259 / 79.6 %); decode 41.3 tok/s (the IQ2 GGUF 28.4 in the same window).
# Switch with ops/use-profile.sh nemotron-bolt-exl3-2.0-hq.
QSE_NH_MODEL=nemotron-3.5-bolt-74b-a9b
QSE_NH_VARIANT=bolt-exl3-2.0-hq
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=23.48
MAX_LEN=262144
# MemAvailable (GiB) a start needs: the weights (20.22 allocated, measured), the engine and its graphs, the
# allocator, the prefill workspace, three slots' KV and the 15 GiB floor
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=50
# the engine's limits. Ceiling: the weights (20.22) + the runtime (an estimate of 4 until measured) + the KV of
# three slots at 262,144 tokens (6); peak: the ceiling + the prefill workspace (an estimate of 4)
MEM_CEILING_GIB=31
MEM_PEAK_GIB=35
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_nemotron.env"
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=0xBakeer/TandemLLM-Nemotron-3.5-Bolt-74B-A9B-EXL3-2.0-hq
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=0c59e1c05ce5d0161028d2a8f7392730ba5d79a2
# Bolt has no MTP head: the lookup cut by StairCut drafts alone
QSE_ENGINE_FLAGS="--model ${QSE_WEIGHTS_DIR} --drafter mtp"
